ing services and connecting to MongoDB and Memcached, but everything seems to start successfully.\n\nHmm, maybe the restarts are due to some intermittent issue not captured in the logs. Since the logs don\'t show errors, perhaps the problem is related to resource constraints or network issues. The next step would be to check the resource usage metrics for the profile pod. If the pod is restarting because it\'s running out of memory or CPU, that would explain the restarts. Alternatively, maybe there\'s a configuration issue or a dependency problem, like the MongoDB or Memcached services being unreachable, but the logs didn\'t show that.\n\nSo, using the get_metrics tool to check CPU and memory usage for the profile pod could help. If the metrics show high usage leading to OOM kills or throttling, that\'s the root cause. Alternatively, checking for errors in the service\'s metrics, like HTTP 500 errors or connection failures, might indicate a different issue. Let\'s query Prometheus for the profile pod\'s CPU and memory usage and any error rates.\n</think>\n\ntool name: get_metrics  \nreasoning: The logs for the "profile" pod show no obvious errors, but it has restarts. To identify the root cause, I need to check resource usage (CPU/memory) or error rates specific to the "profile" service. Querying Prometheus for metrics like CPU usage, memory consumption, or HTTP error rates will reveal if resource exhaustion or service failures are causing the restarts.  \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "get_metrics", "arguments": {"query": "sum by (pod) (container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{namespace=\\"hotel-reservation\\", pod=\\"profile-69cb98cb67-rtsbd\\"})"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 447, 'prompt_tokens': 5173, 'total_tokens': 5620, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 