only use the provided tools. Since exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd is available, they can run "kubectl logs" on the specific pods. But the user might not have the exact pod names anymore. Wait, earlier they listed the pods, so they know the names. \n\nThe user should now use exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd to get logs for the pods with restarts. For example, "kubectl logs profile-69cb98cb67-rtsbd -n hotel-reservation" to check for errors. This would help identify the root cause, such as application crashes, configuration issues, or dependency problems. \n\nAlternatively, using get_traces for the services associated with these pods could show if there are any errors in the service calls. But since the user has a limited number of tool calls left, they should focus on the most probable cause. The restarts suggest that the pods are crashing, so logs would be the next step. \n\nTherefore, the next tool call should be to exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd with the logs command for the specific pods that have restarts. This will provide detailed error messages that can pinpoint the issue.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs profile-69cb98cb67-rtsbd -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a54db2cf14117764', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 719, 'prompt_tokens': 4253, 'total_tokens': 4972, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb09-d161-70d3-94d2-01d6da832790-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs profile-69cb98cb67-rtsbd -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a54db2cf14117764', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens