be to use `get_services` to check if "profile" is present. If it is, then use `get_operations` to find the correct metric names. That way, the user can construct a valid PromQL query. Alternatively, if "profile" isn\'t a service in Grafana, maybe the metrics are under a different name. \n\nTherefore, the next tool to use is `get_services` to verify the service names available, which will help in identifying the correct metrics to query. Once the correct metrics are known, the user can adjust the PromQL query accordingly.\n</think>\n\nget_services  \n**Reasoning**: The previous `get_metrics` query failed due to invalid metric names (`profile_service_errors_total`/`profile_service_latency_seconds`). To resolve this, first confirm if the "profile" service exists in Grafana and identify its associated metrics. This will ensure accurate PromQL queries for error rates or latency.  \n\n**Args**:  \n- No arguments required.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=834, prompt_tokens=2729, total_tokens=3563, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb0b-c0d1-7532-8915-0128ff80c8f4-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2729, 'output_tokens': 834, 'total_tokens': 3563}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='957a34f8-f36e-497b-83e1-6330c62d1497')]]
