ut the service may still have issues. Next, check the associated pods to confirm if the container is crashing or restarting. This will help identify if the problem is with the pod\'s configuration, image, or runtime environment.  \n\n**Args**:  \n- `command`: `kubectl get pods -n hotel-reservation | grep profile`', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=461, prompt_tokens=3767, total_tokens=4228, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb0c-3c42-7612-af0b-9565c87e6e16-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3767, 'output_tokens': 461, 'total_tokens': 4228}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='35b81e2a-9e29-4a31-af53-78fd723fa114')]]
