ints for the services the profile depends on, like MongoDB and Memcached, and those were present. When they described the pod, they saw that the container exited with code 2, which is a generic error. The image used was "yinfangchen/hotelreservation:latest", and it was pulled successfully. \n\nSince there were no specific errors in the logs or metrics, the next step was to consider the container image itself. Exit code 2 can mean different things, but without more info, it\'s hard to tell. The user concluded that the image might be misconfigured or incompatible, leading to silent failures. \n\nSo, the final answer points to the container image as the root cause. The user submitted that the issue is with the image, suggesting it needs re-validation or rebuilding. That makes sense because if the image is broken, the container would fail to start properly, leading to restarts without clear logs. The tools used didn\'t catch the image issue because the logs were silent, so the only clue was the exit code and the restarts.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs profile-69cb98cb67-rtsbd -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b3c4a521025ff194', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 411, 'prompt_tokens': 5781, 'total_tokens': 6192, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb0c-83d5-7db0-a1a4-9390fb8adf4a-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs profile-69cb98cb67-rtsbd -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b3c4a521025ff194', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5781, 'output_tokens': 411, 'total_tokens': 6192}),